{"surah": 103, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "وَٱلْعَصْرِ ", "translation": "By time,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْعَصْرِ", "translit": "ِrْṣَʿعْlٱَw", "root": "عصر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ ", "translation": "Indeed, mankind is in loss,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خُسْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْsُhk", "root": "خسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ ", "translation": "Except for those who have believed and done righteous deeds and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَتَوَاصَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَṣāَwَtَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَتَوَاصَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَṣāَwَtَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِٱلصَّبْرِ", "translit": "ِrْbَّṣlٱِb", "root": "صبر"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "وَمَهْمَا تَمَّتْ مَعْرِفَتُهُ كَانَتِ الْخَشْيَةُ أَغْلَبَ الْأَحْوَالِ عَلَى قَلْبِهِ فَإِنَّ التَّضْيِيقَ غَالِبٌ عَلَى آيَاتِ الْقُرْآنِ فَلَا يَرَى ذِكْرَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ وَالرَّحْمَةِ إِلَّا مُقْرُونًا بِشُرُوطٍ يَقْصُرُ الْعَارِفُ عَنْ نَيْلِهَا كَقَوْلِهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ﴿ وَإِنِّي لَغَفَّارٌ ﴾  {}  ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ ذَلِكَ بِأَرْبَعَةِ شُرُوطٍ ﴿ لِمَنْ تَابَ وَآمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ثُمَّ اهْتَدَى ﴾  {} وَقَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى ﴿ وَالْعَصْرِ إِنَّ الْإِنْسَانَ لَفِي خُسْرٍ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا", "english": "And whenever his knowledge is perfected, the Fear (Khushya) becomes the most dominant state upon his Heart (Qalb), for the restriction is predominant over the verses of the Quran, so he does not see the mention of Forgiveness (Maghfira) and Mercy (Rahma) except coupled with conditions that the Knower (Arif) falls short of attaining, like His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'And indeed, I am Forgiving (Ghaffar)' {} then He followed that with four conditions: 'For whoever repents and believes and does righteous deeds then is guided' {} and His saying, Exalted: 'By the Time (Al-Asr), indeed, mankind is in loss, except those who have believed and done righteous deeds and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience' {} He mentioned four conditions, and where He restricted the mention to a comprehensive condition, He said, Exalted: 'Indeed, the Mercy (Rahma) of Allah is near to the Doers of Good (Muhsinin)' {} so Doing Good (Ihsan) encompasses all, and thus whoever peruses the Quran from its beginning to its end, and whoever understands that, is worthy that his state be Fear (Khushya) and Sorrow (Huzn).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ولنرجع إلى الغرض المطلوب فالمقصود أن غرور الشيطان بأن الآخرة شك يدفع إما بيقين تقليدي، وأما ببصيرة ومشاهدة من جهة الباطن، والمؤمنين بألسنتهم وبعقائدهم إذا ضيعوا أوامر الله تعالى وهجروا الأعمال الصالحة ولابسوا الشهوات والمعاصي فهم مشاركون للكفار في هذا الغرور من النار ولو بعد حين، ولكنهم أيضاً من المغرورين فإنهم اعترفوا بأن الآخرة خير من الدنيا ولكنهم مالوا إلى الدنيا وآثروها، ومجرد الإيمان لا يكفي للفوز قال تعالى \"وإني لغفار لمن تاب وآمن وعمل صالحاً ثم اهتدى\" وقال تعالى \"إن رحمت الله قريب من الم", "english": "And let us return to the intended purpose, so the intended meaning is that the deception of Satan that the Hereafter is doubt is repelled either by traditional certainty, or by insight and witnessing from the aspect of the inner dimension, and the believers with their tongues and with their beliefs if they neglect the commands of Allah the Exalted and abandon righteous works and associate with desires and disobediences, they are partners with the disbelievers in this deception from the Fire even if after a while, but they are also among the deceived for they acknowledged that the Hereafter is better than the worldly life but they inclined to the worldly life and preferred it, and mere faith is not sufficient for success. Allah the Exalted said: \"And indeed, I am Forgiving to whoever repents and believes and does righteous work then is guided\" and Allah the Exalted said: \"Indeed, the mercy of Allah is near to the doers of good\" then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \"Excellence (Ihsan) is that you worship Allah as if you see Him\"[5] and Allah the Exalted said: \"By the time (Al-Asr), indeed, mankind is in loss, except those who have believed and done righteous works and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience.\" So the promise of forgiveness in all the Book of Allah the Exalted is conditional upon faith and righteous work together, not upon faith alone, so these are also deceived, I mean those who are content with the worldly life, joyful in it, luxuriating in its pleasures, loving it. Those who hate death fearing the loss of the delights of the worldly life, not those who hate it fearing what comes after it, so this is an example of deception by the worldly life from the disbelievers and the believers altogether.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-10a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Delusion", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Condemnation of Delusion'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "وأما المعتزلة فشبهتهم قوله تعالى: ﴿ وإني لغفار لمن تاب وآمن وعمل صالحا ثم اهتدى ﴾ {} وقوله تعالى: ﴿ والعصر إن الإنسان لفي خسر إلا الذين آمنوا وعملوا الصالحات ﴾ {} وقوله تعالى ﴿ وإن منكم إلا واردها كان على ربك حتما مقضيا ﴾ {} ثم قال: ﴿ ثم ننجي الذين اتقوا ﴾ {} وقوله تعالى: ﴿ ومن يعص الله ورسوله فإن له نار جهنم ﴾ {} وكل آية ذكر الله عز وجل العمل الصالح فيها مقرونا بالإيمان", "english": "As for the Mu'tazilites, their evidence is His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, I am Forgiving to whoever repents and believes and does righteous deeds then remains guided' and His saying, the Exalted: 'By the Time (Al-'Asr), indeed, the human being (Al-Insan) is in loss (Khusr) except those who have believed and done righteous deeds' and His saying, the Exalted: 'And there is none of you except he will enter it; it has been upon your Lord a decree determined' then He said: 'Then We will save those who feared (Allah) (Ittaqaw)' and His saying, the Exalted: 'And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger, then indeed, for him is the Fire of Hell' and every verse in which Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, mentions righteous deeds (Al-'Amal Al-Salih) therein coupled with faith (Al-Iman).", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-2.doc.txt", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Dhikr"}, {"arabic": "وإن الله عز وجلّ قال: ﴿ والعصر إن الإنسان لفي خسر إلا الذين آمنوا ﴾{} إلى آخرها وإن الأمور تجري بإذن الله فلا يحملنكم استبطاء أمر على استعجاله فإن الله عز وجل لا يعجل لعجلة أحد ومن غالب الله غلبه ومن خادع الله خدعه", "english": "And Allah the Exalted said: 'By the time (Al-Asr), indeed, mankind is in loss (Khusr), except those who have believed (Amanu)' to its end. And matters proceed by the permission of Allah, so do not let the delay of a matter lead you to hasten it, for Allah the Exalted does not hasten for anyone's haste, and whoever contends with Allah is overcome, and whoever deceives Allah is deceived.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "General"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 1667]], "2": [[1, 350, 1439], [2, 1439, 3306], [3, 3306, 4350], [4, 4350, 5304]], "3": [[1, 400, 1063], [2, 1063, 1886], [3, 1886, 2979], [4, 2979, 4116], [5, 4116, 5384], [6, 5384, 6841], [7, 6841, 7642], [8, 7642, 9099], [9, 9099, 10094]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 250, 2683]], "2": [[1, 350, 1777], [2, 1777, 4224], [3, 4224, 5592], [4, 5592, 6843]], "3": [[1, 400, 1686], [2, 1686, 3283], [3, 3283, 5403], [4, 5403, 7608], [5, 7608, 10068], [6, 10068, 12895], [7, 12895, 14450], [8, 14450, 17277], [9, 17277, 19208]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 230, 1550]], "2": [[1, 330, 1369], [2, 1369, 3365], [3, 3365, 4466], [4, 4466, 5460]], "3": [[1, 460, 1349], [2, 1349, 2388], [3, 2388, 4056], [4, 4056, 5748], [5, 5748, 7207], [6, 7207, 9418], [7, 9418, 10292], [8, 10292, 12503], [9, 12503, 13580]]}}, "letterTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"103:1": [{"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 0, "char": "و", "grapheme": "وَ", "start": 250, "end": 587, "duration": 337, "peakTime": 418}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ٱ", "grapheme": "ٱ", "start": 587, "end": 654, "duration": 67, "peakTime": 620}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 2, "char": "ل", "grapheme": "لْ", "start": 654, "end": 879, "duration": 225, "peakTime": 766}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 3, "char": "ع", "grapheme": "عَ", "start": 879, "end": 1149, "duration": 270, "peakTime": 1014}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 4, "char": "ص", "grapheme": "صْ", "start": 1149, "end": 1441, "duration": 292, "peakTime": 1295}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 5, "char": "ر", "grapheme": "رِ", "start": 1441, "end": 1667, "duration": 226, "peakTime": 1554}], "103:2": [{"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 0, "char": "إ", "grapheme": "إِ", "start": 350, "end": 708, "duration": 358, "peakTime": 529}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ن", "grapheme": "نَّ", "start": 708, "end": 1439, "duration": 731, "peakTime": 1074}, {"wordIdx": 1, "charIdx": 0, "char": "ٱ", "grapheme": "ٱ", "start": 1439, "end": 1528, "duration": 89, "peakTime": 1484}, {"wordIdx": 1, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ل", "grapheme": "لْ", "start": 1528, "end": 1826, "duration": 298, "peakTime": 1677}, {"wordIdx": 1, "charIdx": 2, "char": "إ", "grapheme": "إِ", "start": 1826, "end": 2184, "duration": 358, "peakTime": 2005}, {"wordIdx": 1, "charIdx": 3, "char": "ن", "grapheme": "ن", "start": 2184, "end": 2482, "duration": 298, "peakTime": 2333}, {"wordIdx": 1, "charIdx": 4, "char": "س", "grapheme": "سَٰ", "start": 2482, "end": 3007, "duration": 525, "peakTime": 2744}, {"wordIdx": 1, "charIdx": 5, "char": "ن", "grapheme": "نَ", "start": 3007, "end": 3306, "duration": 299, "peakTime": 3156}, {"wordIdx": 2, "charIdx": 0, "char": "ل", "grapheme": "لَ", "start": 3306, "end": 3604, "duration": 298, "peakTime": 3455}, {"wordIdx": 2, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ف", "grapheme": "فِ", "start": 3604, "end": 3902, "duration": 298, "peakTime": 3753}, {"wordIdx": 2, "charIdx": 2, "char": "ى", "grapheme": "ى", "start": 3902, "end": 4350, "duration": 448, "peakTime": 4126}, {"wordIdx": 3, "charIdx": 0, "char": "خ", "grapheme": "خُ", "start": 4350, "end": 4678, "duration": 328, "peakTime": 4514}, {"wordIdx": 3, "charIdx": 1, "char": "س", "grapheme": "سْ", "start": 4678, "end": 5006, "duration": 328, "peakTime": 4842}, {"wordIdx": 3, "charIdx": 2, "char": "ر", "grapheme": "رٍ", "start": 5006, "end": 5304, "duration": 298, "peakTime": 5155}], "103:3": [{"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 0, "char": "إ", "grapheme": "إِ", "start": 400, "end": 575, "duration": 175, "peakTime": 488}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ل", "grapheme": "لَّ", "start": 575, "end": 830, "duration": 255, "peakTime": 702}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 2, "char": "ا", "grapheme": "ا", "start":